# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NOT PUBLISHED. These stay on disk and out of the repository.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# `concordance/` and `audit/` are internal BY CONSTRUCTION, not by preference:
# both hardcode a path into the private product repository and import from its
# application code, so they could not run for anyone else even if published. The
# concordance ARTIFACT is the public thing; the pipeline that derives it from our
# corpus is not, and the distinction is the same one the registry draws when it
# says nobody should need our data to use this scheme.
#
# `PLAN.md` and `research/06-community/` are commercial: competitive analysis,
# what to budget this as, and which organisations to approach. Publishing a
# target list alongside an invitation to adopt would be its own answer.
#
# A file listed here can still be forced in with `git add -f`. Do not.
PLAN.md
research/
audit/
concordance/

# Build artifacts of a full corpus run.
#
# `concordance.jsonl.gz` is the artifact intended for CC0 publication, but it is
# 125 MB and rebuilt from the corpus, so it is released, not committed.
#
# `ledger.jsonl.gz` is INTERNAL and must not be published as-is. It is a gap
# register: it names internal act_ids, enumerates the documents we hold but
# cannot address, and lists the corpora where our provenance is missing or
# non-official. That is the same class of artifact as the US corpus gap register,
# which was decided to stay internal. Publish counts and classes from the
# manifest, never the register itself.
concordance/dist/

# The resolver index: 1.8 GB of SQLite, rebuilt from the concordance by
# `resolver/build_index.py` in a few minutes. Released alongside the concordance
# for anyone who wants to run their own resolver without rebuilding, never
# committed. It is derived data and contains nothing the concordance does not.
resolver/dist/
